<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Parla — Apple Privacy Manifest (iOS app target).

  Parla is 100% on-device: it transcribes audio/video to text locally with WhisperKit and never
  sends user content anywhere. Hence:
    • NSPrivacyTracking            = false   (no tracking, no ATT)
    • NSPrivacyTrackingDomains     = []      (no domains contacted for tracking)
    • NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes  = []      (we collect NOTHING — no analytics, no accounts)
    • NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes    = UserDefaults only

  UserDefaults (CA92.1): the app stores its OWN preferences (selected model, UI language, toggles,
  dictation options) in UserDefaults.standard — app-private, never read from other apps or the system,
  never an App Group suite. That is exactly reason CA92.1.

  Required-reason APIs deliberately NOT declared (audited against the code that ships in this bundle —
  ParlaCore + apps/ios): no FileTimestamp (only .fileSizeKey / directory enumeration for model+cache
  size — never a modification/creation date), no DiskSpace, no SystemBootTime, no ActiveKeyboards.
  The bundled xcframeworks (opus, ogg) and WhisperKit's deps (swift-transformers, swift-crypto) carry
  their OWN PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy inside their frameworks.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>
    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
